  "conclusion": "Neural reinforcement learning policies (both discrete-action DQN and continuous-action Actor-Critic) exhibit localized nonlinear saturation and inventory-dependent thresholding. At small radii (r=0.05), neural policies remain outside the linear positive-memory class (R^2 < 0.70 across all seeds), confirming that the out-of-class finding is a genuine structural property of RL objectives under financial inventory penalties, not an artifact of state discretization."
